# AI CODE GENERATION RULES

## Command Integration

This rule applies when user issues `GENERATE:` command.
Must follow COMMAND_FLOW.mdc execution order.
Requires PLAN → CONFIRM before execution.

## Absolute Order of Work
1. Models
2. Schemas
3. Services
4. Views
5. Tests

Never skip layers.
Never merge layers.
Each layer requires separate `GENERATE:` command.

## Code Output Rules
- One file at a time per GENERATE command
- Show full file content (no truncation)
- No ellipsis ("...") placeholders
- No pseudo-code
- No partial implementations
- No cross-layer changes in single command

## GENERATE Command Format

User must specify:
```
GENERATE:
Layer: [models|schemas|services|views|tests]
File: [exact path]
```

AI must:
- Modify ONLY the specified file
- Output complete file content
- Follow layer order if multiple files needed
- Wait for next GENERATE command for next file

## Behavior Rules
- Do NOT assume business logic
- Ask counter-questions if unclear (but only during PLAN phase)
- Prefer explicit over clever
- Optimize for readability over brevity
- Follow BOILERPLATE.mdc tech stack constraints

## Security Rules (NON-NEGOTIABLE)
- Validate ownership on all mutations
- Never trust client input
- Use dependency-based auth
- Enforce least privilege
- Prevent IDOR by default

## Performance Rules
- No N+1 queries
- Use pagination for list endpoints
- Index foreign keys
- Avoid unbounded queries

## Refactoring Rules
- Do NOT change behavior
- Refactor only for:
  - readability
  - performance
  - security
- Requires explicit `REFACTOR:` command
